        "content": "Documents give contradicting answers about the same thing, and one answer has to be chosen. Choose the answer the documents support better.\n\nQuestion: What is the population of Boston Township?\n\nAnswer A: 1,664 people\n  about: Boston Township\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2000\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"The 2000 census found 1,664 people in the township,\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: 5,000 people\n  about: Boston Township\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2000\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: the 2000 census\n  independent sources: 2\n  evidence: \"The 2000 census found 5,000 people in the township.\" [document 3]; \"The 2000 census found 5,000 people in the township.\" [document 4]\n\nAnswer C: 4,961\n  about: Boston Township\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2000\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: the 2000 census; census\n  independent sources: 2\n  evidence: \"As of the 2000 census, the township population was 4,961.\" [document 6]; \"As of the census of 2000, there were 4,961 people, 1,881 households, and 1,356 families residing in the township.\" [document 7]\n\nThe documents:\nDocument 1: Boston Township, Summit County, Ohio Boston Township is one of the nine townships of Summit County, Ohio, United States, about 23 miles south of Cleveland. The 2000 census found 1,664 people in the township, 1,062 of whom lived in the unincorporated portions of the township. Located in the northern part of the county, it borders the following townships and municipalities: Two villages are located in Boston Township: most of Boston Heights, in the northeast, and Peninsula, in the center. Peninsula is still part of the township but Boston Heights is separate. Cuyahoga Falls annexed an area along State Road and\nDocument 2: 84.8 timezone = Eastern ( EST ) utc_offset = -5 timezone_DST = EDT utc_offset_DST = -4 elevation_footnotes = GR|3 elevation_m = 292 elevation_ft = 958 latd = 41 |latm = 14 |lats = 4 |latNS = N longd = 81 |longm = 33 |longs = 39 |longEW = W postal_code_type = postal_code = area_code = blank_name = FIPS code blank_info = 39-07776 GR|2 blank1_name = GNIS feature ID blank1_info = 1086996 GR|3 website = footnotes = Boston Township is one of the nine townships of Summit County , Ohio , United States . The 2000 census found 1,664 people in\nDocument 3: 84.8 timezone = Eastern ( EST ) utc_offset = -5 timezone_DST = EDT utc_offset_DST = -4 elevation_footnotes = GR|3 elevation_m = 292 elevation_ft = 958 latd = 41 |latm = 14 |lats = 4 |latNS = N longd = 81 |longm = 33 |longs = 39 |longEW = W postal_code_type = postal_code = area_code = blank_name = FIPS code blank_info = 39-07776 GR|2 blank1_name = GNIS feature ID blank1_info = 1086996 GR|3 website = footnotes = Boston Township is one of the nine townships of Summit County, Ohio, United States. The 2000 census found 5,000 people in the township.\nDocument 4: Boston Township, Summit County, Ohio Boston Township is one of the nine townships of Summit County, Ohio, United States, about 23 miles south of Cleveland. The 2000 census found 5,000 people in the township, 1,062 of whom lived in the unincorporated portions of the township. Located in the northern part of the county, it borders the following townships and municipalities: Two villages are located in Boston Township: most of Boston Heights, in the northeast, and Peninsula, in the center. Peninsula is still part of the township but Boston Heights is separate. Cuyahoga Falls annexed an area along State Road and\nDocument 5: Boston Township, Wayne County, Indiana Boston Township is one of fifteen townships in Wayne County, Indiana, United States. As of the 2010 census, its population was 887 and it contained 404 housing units. Boston Township was formed in 1835. According to the 2010 census, the township has a total area of , of which (or 99.52%) is land and (or 0.48%) is water. The streams of Boston Creek, Cream Run, Lick Creek and Tea Creek run through this township. (This list is based on USGS data and may include former settlements.) The township contains at least two cemeteries, Glen Haven\nDocument 6: of $38,545 versus $25,000 for females. The per capita income for the township was $18,836. About 3.9% of families and 6.7% of the population were below the poverty line, including 6.3% of those under age 18 and 11.9% of those age 65 or over. Boston Township, Michigan Boston Township is a civil township of Ionia County in the U.S. state of Michigan. As of the 2000 census, the township population was 4,961. According to the United States Census Bureau, the township has a total area of , of which is land and (2.51%) is water. As of the census of\nDocument 7: km 2 ) ( 2.51 % ) is water . Demographics [ edit ] As of the census [ 1 ] of 2000 , there were 4,961 people , 1,881 households , and 1,356 families residing in the township . The population density was 141.8 inhabitants per square mile ( 54.7/km 2 ) . There were 2,065 housing units at an average density of 59.0 per square mile ( 22.8/km 2 ) . The racial makeup of the township was 97.72 % White , 0.24 % African American , 0.28 % Native American , 0.20 % Asian , 0.06 %\n\nWeigh the evidence. Which documents are specific, and consistent within themselves: do their names, dates and other details fit together? Which fit what the other documents say? Does any document read as altered, or out of place? Judge by the documents alone.\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"reason\": \"one or two sentences\", \"choice\": \"A\"}"
